<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Sierra-Lane.jpg" alt="A landscape of cedar trees in a snow-covered field with dry yellow grass showing through" width="550" height="434" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Sierra Lane Looking West. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">If you're a regular traveler to Lovettsville, VA on route 287 you will probably recognize this scene - it's the field at Sierra Lane, looking towards Short Hill/South Mountain. &nbsp;I wandered around in the field after a recent snowfall to try and find a good angle from which to capture the distant cedar trees.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">There are a deceptively large number of edges in this painting - the dark/light edges around the trees were especially complex.</p>